module std where

-- ifElse — polymorphic conditional. ∀a. Boolean → a → a → a.
--
-- The clause LHS is the bare `ifElse` (id `std:ifElse`).
-- Phase 5b8's `ifElseFn` divergence + the std.ts
-- `f.id === "std-ifElse:ifElseFn"` extraction seam are
-- RETIRED by FM-retire-9 9a (the `…Fn` clauses renamed
-- to their bare ids). No `@codeName`. (`ifElse` was
-- never a parser keyword anyway; the param rename below
-- is the load-bearing part that stays.)
--
-- Pre-5b8 the spec params were `condition, then,
-- else`. The `then` / `else` idents are parser
-- reserved keywords (KW set in parser-keywords.ts);
-- the body can't reference `{var: "then"}` / `{var:
-- "else"}` directly via .fenel source. 5b8 renames
-- the SPEC params themselves to `condition,
-- consequent, alternative` — a NEW workaround tier
-- beyond 5b6/5b7's .fenel-ident divergence (the
-- spec's own params change). Consequence-free since
-- pre-5b8 grep confirmed no named-arg callers use
-- `then` / `else` keys.
--
-- Pre-5b8 the spec was TS-native via
-- `stdNatives.ifElse = (cond, then, els) => cond ?
-- then : els` at engine/src/modules/std.ts:3235.
-- Post-5b8 the spec gains a body and the
-- `stdNatives.ifElse` entry is deleted.
--
-- The body uses the canonical lazy if-form, but an ordinary function call
-- evaluates its arguments before entering that body. Both consequent and
-- alternative are already values here. For branch expressions that perform
-- effects or may fail, use `if condition then expression else expression`
-- at the call site so only the selected expression is evaluated.
--
-- If-lowering source-of-truth migration (5b5 numeric
-- comparators via min/max → 5b6 Boolean short-circuits
-- via and/or → 5b7 Boolean negation via not → 5b8
-- polymorphic conditional via ifElse). The named-op-key
-- dispatch path (via `stdNatives.ifElse`) is retired;
-- `ifElse` calls dispatch through the function registry
-- to the if-form body.

@label "If-else"
@description "Choose between two already evaluated values. ∀a. Boolean → a → a → a. Function arguments are eager; use the structural if form when only the selected branch expression should evaluate."
@tags "control"
ifElse : (condition: Boolean) -> (consequent: a) -> (alternative: a) -> a
ifElse condition consequent alternative = if condition then consequent else alternative
